   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INTRODUCTION:
Novel Association for Youth Advocacy is a non-governmental, not-for profit organization registered in Nigeria in 2014. Its goal is to galvanize coalitions of youth-led organizations in Nigeria, to create an enabling policy environment thatfosters the wellbeing and rights of young people. The network has 15 member organizations spread across 6 States of Nigeria, and over 45 youthadvocates trained on policy dialogue, reforms &lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;)&gt;)&gt; implementation.

